=== Background information ===
Including Arex in ''[[Star Trek: The Animated Series|The Animated Series]]'' accomplished two goals: it provided variety with yet another "[[alien]]" crewmember that an animated series could afford, and it replaced [[Pavel Chekov]] without employing an additional actor. Arex is the first wholly non-Human Starfleet officer to appear on screen.

Although Arex is clearly shown to be a navigator, production art sketches of Arex described him as the [[helmsman]]. (''[[Star Trek: The Official Guide to the Animated Series]]'', pp. 28, 46-47) Additionally, the final draft script of {{e|Mudd's Passion}} refers to him as "the alternate helmsman". In the same script, Arex is also described as "''male, but his voice has a soft, musical tone... on the tenor side.''" {{Audio|file=Arex.ogg|text=Said voice}} was provided by [[James Doohan]].

According to [[StarTrek.com]], {{st.com|bl=1|archivedate=20230000000000|database_article/chekov-pavel-animated-series}} Arex was Pavel Chekov's navigation instructor at [[Starfleet Academy]]. This information comes from a 1973 newsletter by [[Gene Roddenberry]] and [[D.C. Fontana]], which described the ''Animated Series'' in general, and gave detailed bios of Arex and [[M'Ress]]. It also states Arex is a veteran and known as the best navigator in Starfleet. He began his career as a technician serving on merchant vessels, and not going through Starfleet Academy, he became an officer via "[[field commission]]". "''While Arex appears to be a quiet, efficient, junior officer, Captain Kirk knows the Lieutenant is entitled to wear three decorations for bravery and has a Starfleet Citation for Conspicuous Valor. Arex himself would never mention them.''" {{el|startrekanimated.com/tas_news_mress_arex_bio.html}}

In {{VST|Walk, Don't Run}}, he was voiced by [[Carlos Alazraqui]].

=== Apocrypha ===
Arex appeared briefly in the [[novels]] ''[[The Galactic Whirlpool]]'', ''[[Time for Yesterday]]'', ''[[The Fire and the Rose]]'', and the graphic novel version of ''{{dis|The Ashes of Eden|comic}}''. He made several appearances in the first volume of [[Star Trek (DC volume 1)|DC's ''Star Trek'' comics]], which were set after {{film|4}}.

Arex became a minor character in the ''[[Star Trek: New Frontier]]'' series, where in [[2305]], he was aboard a shuttlecraft that fell through a [[wormhole]] and was thrown 71 years into the future to [[2376]]. After spending a brief time with the [[Department of Temporal Investigations]]' Temporal Displacement Division, he later became a [[security officer]] aboard the USS ''Trident'' under the command of Captain [[Elizabeth Shelby|Shelby]]. In these novels, his full name is given as "Arex Na Eth".

Arex's [[homeworld]] [[Edos]] was first mentioned in [[Lincoln Enterprises]] publicity material in 1974. Arex is referred to as an "Edoan" in [[Alan Dean Foster]]'s ''Star Trek Log'' series of novelizations. According to the ''Star Trek: New Frontier'' novels, Arex is described as a Triexian, a species sometimes mistaken for Edosians. ''[[The Latter Fire]]'' also corroborates this. ''The Latter Fire'' also established that Arex joined the ''Enterprise'' crew in [[2269]] on [[Stardate]] 5371.3 after transferring over from the USS ''Arcadia'' just prior to the ''Enterprise''{{'}}s mission to the Syhaari star system that year.

Arex's biography on [[StarTrek.com]] describes him as an only child, but the novel ''[[Cold Wars]]'' describes him as part of a very large family with eleven brothers and thirteen sisters.

In [[IDW Publishing]]'s comics, Arex is telepathic.

==== ''very Short Treks'' ====
[[File:Bridge crew (Skin a Cat).jpg|thumb|Arex with Scott during the Klingon attack]]
According to an unreliable and unverified account, a [[fleet]] of {{class|D7}} [[battle cruiser]]s [[attack]]ed the {{USS|Enterprise|NCC-1701}}.

According to an anything but canon account, Arex was present on the [[bridge]] of the [[starship|ship]] when this was occurring. The [[Enterprise captain 001|captain]] was attempting to give the [[crew]] [[order]]s that would help save them from the [[Klingon]]s' continuous [[attack|assault]], but unfortunately, he continued using [[figure of speech|figures of speech]] that [[anger]]ed various [[crewmember]]s.

As a result, the ''Enterprise'' [[explosion|exploded]] due to continuous bombardment from [[disruptor blast]]s. ({{VST|Skin a Cat}})

[[File:Tendi, Arex, Scotty and M'Ress.jpg|thumb|Arex along with Tendi, Scotty and M'Ress]]
According to another anything but canon account, during a [[celebration]] of the fiftieth [[anniversary]] of the [[TOS era|TOS]] [[crew]]'s [[cartoon]] [[show]], Arex was present at this [[party]]. It started off okay, but the three [[Starfleet]] [[officer]]s soon become offended with something that [[D'Vana Tendi]] said, that was clearly a misunderstanding. They were under the impression that she believed that they only [[walking|walked]] while the [[USS Cerritos]] crew [[running|ran]]. Arex told her that he had three [[leg]]s, and as such, he was very good at [[running]].

When [[William T. Riker]] and [[Hikaru Sulu]] exit the [[turbolift]] and step onto the [[bridge]], the [[argument]] begins to calm down, and they all decide to [[Play (activity)|play]] a [[song]] in the style of the ''[[Post Mainframe Acid-Cardassian Ten Forwardcore]]'' [[genre]]. Arex plays the [[double guitar]], while [[William T. Riker]] [[singing|sings]] and plays the [[trombone]]. [[Hikaru Sulu]] also sang, and played the [[electronic keyboard|keyboard]], [[M'Ress]] played the [[tambourine]] and [[Montgomery Scott|Scotty]] played the [[drum]]s.

They were so [[euphoria|euphoric]] playing their song, that they didn't even notice that they were under [[attack]] by a [[fleet]] of [[Klingon]] [[D7 class|battle cruisers]]. Although Tendi did quickly notice it, and at that point so did everyone else when there was an [[explosion]] on the [[bridge]]. ({{VST|Walk, Don't Run}})

